## Subject: `mixbench` — GPU/CPU roofline micro-benchmark suite

The repo (`ekondis/mixbench`) builds **five independent single-file executables**, one per CMake subproject. Each measures the compute/memory-bandwidth trade-off of a *single* compute device. None use MPI, NCCL/RCCL, parallel I/O, checkpointing, or any launcher — they all run as a plain single-process binary that prints CSV to stdout. They are distinct applications from a scheduler's view, so I recorded a separate trace for each.

### Traces recorded

| Variant | Executable | Parallelism | Accelerator | Placement notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **cuda** | `mixbench-cuda [GPU_ID]` | GPU | CUDA | One GPU (arg default 0); single node; no multi-GPU/gpu_comm |
| **hip** | `mixbench-hip` | GPU | ROCm/HIP | Hardwired to device 0; single node |
| **sycl** | `mixbench-sycl [idx]` | GPU | SYCL | One device from `sycl::device::get_devices()` by index |
| **opencl** | `mixbench-opencl` | GPU | OpenCL | Single selected device |
| **cpu-openmp** | `mixbench-cpu [size_MB]` | threaded (OpenMP) | none | All cores (`omp_get_max_threads`), SIMD, first-touch → **NUMA-sensitive**, wants a full node (pack) |

### Key evidence
- **No inter-process communication**: search for `MPI_/mpi.h/nccl/rccl/mpirun/srun` returned zero hits — all `communication.model = none`, `launcher = none`.
- **GPU variants** each select exactly one device (`cudaSetDevice(gpu_id)` default 0 / `hipSetDevice(0)` / `sycl::device::get_devices().at(index-1)`) → `multi_gpu = false`, `gpu_comm = none`, `topology.span = single_node`.
- **CPU variant** is OpenMP-threaded (`#pragma omp parallel for`, `omp_get_max_threads`), 64-byte aligned buffer with `#pragma omp simd`, `-march=native`, and a first-touch initialization loop → NUMA-sensitive and effectively wants exclusive cores on one node for peak-bandwidth measurement.

All variants are single-node, no checkpoint, no parallel-I/O library. Confidence is high for the mechanical facts (parallelism model, accelerator kind, single-device, no MPI); the placement/co-location judgments are medium.
